            <div xml:id="d346">

                <pb facs="0379" n="375" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg375"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.001/521: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-03-09T19:00:00-05:00">March 9, 1939—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>54. Your 123, March 8, 4 p.m., trade restrictions in North China. The Department
                    is inclined to agree with your view but raises for your consideration the
                    question whether or not the reasons in favor of an informal approach are
                    outweighed by the desirability of going along with the British wherever
                    practicable in cases where no conflict of principle is involved. The Department
                    desires that you exercise your discretion in the matter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
